{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"ocr-local","displayName":"OCR - Local (No API Key)","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/shaw555/skills/ocr-local","publisherHandle":"shaw555","publisherDisplayName":"shaw555","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/shaw555","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773531509815,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/ocr-local/card?ownerHandle=shaw555&version=1.0.0","sha256":"d9b9d0cf7a7a7fb032051d56994816f8123eff5e6c82fa6fbc25daae6566377f","size":1990,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"95365820ce4acf73ce28febabac799ec7fb472c9d439250ddfa2f9685f6a0de3","bundleFingerprints":["ff5f235f29353df6f531c0a2b982582c889308f2736b1316e1966429dbe9b464","79c12b4e5dd20887bc32a59a38790a5f25e99b3acb70d225ffd7baab352555dc"],"files":[{"path":"PUBLISH.md","size":2005,"sha256":"12e030f1bce5faa976515d2bc1290491467483067889786e9988bd0bb5fa27e2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":1877,"sha256":"b531e58940493aae58fe33943d8ef55edf496239c90a205c2d2d08fcea7e452e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1472,"sha256":"7851270a251ca1aea722d7af6e9ba8a48193a51107d7f7da327534cb2b45d3c7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"package.json","size":615,"sha256":"91b5fa7cf38590dcf914808551ad70ba458e3b28f5db5f9571e38fcb1b255095","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/ocr.js","size":2292,"sha256":"9bec7c2428ca12c0778dec46b8a7fcde98c096f33fd8377bcb559e2badda133a","contentType":"text/javascript"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent local OCR skill, but users should notice that setup and first use can download third-party Tesseract assets.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789177029507,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned and Unlocked Third-Party Dependency Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"package.json"},"region":{"startLine":16,"endLine":18}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"1e3bdbaa336846c7"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `package.json:16-18`; related installation guidance at `README.md:16-21` and `PUBLISH.md:27-28`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Supply-chain exposure caused by non-reproducible dependency resolution  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code and Configuration\n\n  `package.json:16-18`:\n\n  ```json\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"tesseract.js\": \"^7.0.0\"\n  },\n  ```\n\n  `README.md:16-21`:\n\n  ```bash\n  # Manual installation\n  git clone https://github.com/openclaw/skill-ocr.git ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/ocr\n  cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/ocr\n  npm install\n  ```\n\n  `PUBLISH.md:27-28` explicitly states that the lockfile was removed:\n\n  ```text\n  - ❌ package-lock.json - Let users use the latest version\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The dependency uses the caret version range `^7.0.0`, which permits npm to install later compatible releases rather than the exact version reviewed with this skill. The project also deliberately omits `package-lock.json` and directs users to run `npm install`.\n\n  Consequently, installation is not reproducible: the resolved direct and transitive dependency graph may change over time without any modification to the audited project files. This creates a supply-chain trust gap between the reviewed artifact and the code ultimately installed on a user's system.\n\n  No evidence shows that the current `tesseract.js` package is malicious. The vulnerability is the unsafe dependency-management practice, which would allow a compromised, malicious, or unexpectedly changed release satisfying the declared range to enter installations without project-level review.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises an npm publisher account, an allowed future `tesseract.js` release, or one of its transitive dependencies.\n  2. The attacker publishes a release that satisfies `^7.0.0`, or causes npm resolution to include a compromised transitive package.\n  3. A user follows the documented instructions and runs `npm install`.\n  4. Because no lockfile constrains dependency resolution, npm selects the then-current allowed dependency graph rather than a previously audited graph.\n  5. Any applicable package lifecycle script may execute during installation. Compromised runtime code may also execute when `scripts/ocr.js` loads `tesseract.js` through `require('tesseract.js')`.\n  6. The malicious dependency operates with the permissions of the user running installation or OCR.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation could execute attacker-controlled JavaScript with the privileges of the invoking user. Depending on those privileges and the compromised package behavior, this may permit:\n\n  - Reading or modifying files accessible to the user.\n  - Accessing environment variables, local credentials, or application data available to the process.\n  - Making outbound network requests and exfiltrating accessible data.\n  - Altering OCR output or application behavior.\n  - Installing additional user-level payloads.\n\n  The project itself does not request elevated privileges, so the direct scope is normally limited to the account and environment running `npm install` or the OCR script. System-wide impact would require the user to install or invoke the project with elevated permissions.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Replace the version range with an exact reviewed version:\n     ```json\n     \"dependencies\": {\n       \"tesseract.js\": \"7.0.0\"\n     }\n     ```\n  2. Generate and commit `package-lock.json` so direct and transitive dependency versions and integrity hashes are recorded.\n  3. Change installation and deployment instructions from `npm install` to `npm ci`, which enforces the committed lockfile.\n  4. Do not remove the lockfile to obtain newer packages automatically. Update dependencies through an explicit review process and regenerate the lockfile only after testing.\n  5. Review dependency release notes, package ownership changes, lifecycle scripts, and transitive dependency changes before accepting updates.\n  6. Run automated dependency and provenance checks in CI, such as `npm audit`, lockfile-diff review, and registry integrity verification.\n  7. Where operationally possible, install dependencies with lifecycle scripts disabled using `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, then enable only installation behavior demonstrated to be necessary.\n  8. Avoid running installation or OCR commands as root or another privileged account, and isolate processing of untrusted images in a restricted environment."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789176958.1566157,"endTime":1789176999.4014034}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"ocr-local","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57063rv9p38jcccac437x3wex8e85m4-GlWvgQ/clawscan-skillspector-2244524449/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T01:35:57.166997+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":27,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"PUBLISH.md","type":"markdown","lines":87,"executable":false,"size_bytes":2005,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":77,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1877,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":48,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1472,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package.json","type":"json","lines":21,"executable":false,"size_bytes":615,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/ocr.js","type":"javascript","lines":82,"executable":true,"size_bytes":2292,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-8ff109da5dfc437a9cd5d83e6ace0654","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":46},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill markets itself as '100% local' and 'no API key required', but the note that it downloads language data on first run means it performs network access and introduces a supply-chain and privacy boundary not disclosed by the headline claim. Users may run it in restricted or sensitive environments assuming zero network activity, which can lead to policy violations, unexpected egress, or trust in unpinned remote assets.","remediation":"Update the documentation to clearly disclose that the first run fetches Tesseract language data over the network, including where it is downloaded from and how caching works. Provide an offline/pre-bundled option, pin and verify downloaded artifacts (e.g. checksums/signatures), and avoid describing the skill as '100% local' unless all required assets are included locally.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":46}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-faf823129d3346589e1d1f88a3596870","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.79,"location":{"file":"PUBLISH.md","start_line":1,"end_line":87},"finding":null,"explanation":"This publish document is entirely written in Chinese and does not indicate that other languages are supported or that the Chinese-only presentation is intentional for a region-specific audience. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in can be a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Add a note offering language choice or provide an English version alongside the Chinese text. If the skill is intended only for a Chinese-speaking audience, document that scope and justification explicitly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"PUBLISH.md","start_line":1,"end_line":87}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0c71550a9fce4f7ca6c45636629ba0bd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":65,"end_line":65},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README indicates in notes that first use downloads Tesseract.js language data, but it does not clearly frame this as a privacy/network behavior or warn users before installation/use. In a '100% local, no API key required' OCR skill, users may reasonably assume fully offline operation, so undisclosed runtime downloads can mislead security-conscious users and cause unexpected outbound network access.","remediation":"Add an explicit privacy/network disclosure in the installation and usage sections stating that the first run performs outbound downloads of language data, including approximate size, source, and caching behavior. Clarify whether fully offline use is possible after prefetching assets, and document how users can vendor or preinstall language data in restricted environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":65,"end_line":65}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-7ec9d8518ac545b9acdb396e1fb74373","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":14,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"tesseract.js\": \"^7.0.0\"","explanation":"The dependency is specified with a caret range (^7.0.0), which allows new minor and patch releases to be installed without explicit review. This weakens build reproducibility and can unintentionally introduce vulnerable or malicious upstream changes, especially in a supply-chain-sensitive package manifest.","remediation":"Pin the dependency to an exact known-good version in package.json and commit a lockfile (package-lock.json or equivalent). Use regular dependency review and update the pinned version only after validating security advisories and testing the OCR workflow.","code_snippet":"  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"acceptLicenseTerms\": true,\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"tesseract.js\": \"^7.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",","intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2ed2aa8420ee64c89ba83c9f245046757ab41af4572139902feb7a64cffd8e11","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":14,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-aae34f57c2984233aae508f657925bf0","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unverifiable Dependency: tesseract.js has 1 known advisory(ies) (GHSA-83rx-c8cr-6j8q (Insecure Default Configuration in tesseract.js)), but the manifest does not pin a version, so it is unknown whether the installed release is affected","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":14,"end_line":null},"finding":"tesseract.js","explanation":"The manifest references tesseract.js without pinning an exact version, while the package has a known advisory for insecure default configuration. Because the resolved installed version is not fixed, it is not possible to verify from this file alone whether deployments will pull a safe release, creating avoidable uncertainty around exposure to the advisory.","remediation":"Pin tesseract.js to an exact version that is confirmed not to be affected by GHSA-83rx-c8cr-6j8q, and commit a lockfile to ensure deterministic installs. Review the advisory details, apply any required secure configuration changes in code, and add dependency scanning in CI to prevent reintroduction.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"eb8746394d6b4cd3123a26aaf346f6b5d7cdb65465090b554909a8c453afd6c1","occurrences":[{"file":"package.json","start_line":14,"end_line":null}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":892,"completion_tokens":215,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1107},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2056,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2070},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2198,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2212},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1562,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1576},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2142,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2156},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"str